# /root/.ssh/authorized_keys on each SIGNER box.
#
# Capability keys are each pinned to ONE forced-command. A forced-command ignores whatever
# the client asks to run and runs ONLY the named program, so each key's authority
# is exactly one capability and nothing else (no shell, no scp, no port-forward).
#
# 1) The MINTER's key -> can request only token-mint signatures. This is
#    the only key that can cause a mint, and even it is gated by the signer's
#    independent re-derivation + caps + the watchtower heartbeat.
#    Production additionally requires this host to be the one signer named by
#    the root-owned mode-0600 active-mint-signer marker and to obtain a durable
#    receipt from the shared witness before signing. See
#    MINT-SIGNER-WITNESS-RUNBOOK.md; never install this key on two active hosts.
command="/usr/bin/python3 /opt/veld-signer/veld_signerd.py --capability mint",no-pty,no-port-forwarding,no-X11-forwarding,no-agent-forwarding,restrict ssh-ed25519 AAAA...MINTER_PUBKEY... minter@custody-box

# 2) The C1 reservation coordinator's DISTINCT SSH key -> can request only C1
#    RESERVE/EXPOSE/CANCEL/FUND carrier signatures and durable acknowledgements.
#    Never reuse the minter SSH private key for this capability: the two forced
#    commands are intentionally separate authority channels even when installed
#    on the same isolated signer host.
command="/usr/bin/python3 /opt/veld-signer/veld_signerd.py --capability c1-reservation",no-pty,no-port-forwarding,no-X11-forwarding,no-agent-forwarding,restrict ssh-ed25519 AAAA...C1_RESERVATION_COORDINATOR_PUBKEY... c1-reservationd@coordinator

# Each threshold custody signer is a separate host/key share with its own Veld
# node and durable accepted-obligation index. The coordinator key can only invoke
# the root-owned wallet-unlocking policy wrapper; it cannot request a shell or
# forward traffic. Never point this key directly at veld_payout_signerd.py: the
# wrapper sources the required root-owned Veld environment, unlocks for one
# request, and re-locks the wallet on every exit path.
command="/opt/veld-signer/sign-wrapper.sh",no-pty,no-port-forwarding,no-X11-forwarding,no-agent-forwarding,restrict ssh-ed25519 AAAA...REDEEM_COORDINATOR_PUBKEY... redeemd@coordinator

# 3) The WATCHTOWER's key -> can ONLY pause/HALT (runs veld_wt_recv.py). It can
#    write a heartbeat or set HALT; it can NEVER sign, read the key, or run a
#    shell. So granting the watchtower a way to stop minting does NOT grant it any
#    way to cause minting.
command="/usr/bin/python3 /opt/veld-signer/veld_wt_recv.py",no-pty,no-port-forwarding,no-X11-forwarding,no-agent-forwarding,restrict ssh-ed25519 AAAA...WATCHTOWER_PUBKEY... veldwt@watchtower-box
#
# Beat signature pin: veld_wt_recv.py additionally requires every beat to
# carry a valid ML-DSA signature from the watchtower's dedicated beat-signing key
# (separate from the SSH key above). Pin that key's PUBLIC hex on this box at
#    /opt/veld-signer/watchtower-beat-pubkey.hex
# (from `veld-keygen show <watchtower beat.key> --full-pubkey-hex`). veld-keygen must
# be present beside veld_wt_recv.py. If the pin is absent the receiver FAILS CLOSED
# (rejects every beat -> signer goes stale -> refuses to sign). A dev/regtest signer
# may bypass by touching /opt/veld-signer/beat-unsigned-ok.
